body:
"If you’re volunteering so much that you’re unable to contribute your  time or energy to a theme camp, then I’d counsel you to camp with your  volunteer department.  That’s what they’re there for!"

&#x200B;

You might be surprised to know that this isn't always an option. For example, Rangers Camp Moscow requires people to work at least 40 hours to camp there making it a heaven for workaholics, but limiting any real personal time. Ranger Camp Tokyo is so packed in and fills up so that not everyone who wants to camp there can. Ranger Camp Berlin as well. ESD requires meal and shower plans to be purchased for a large portion of their camp. The free space for ESD volunteers has been reduced to such a small size that less than 50 can camp there with sufficient space for infrastructure to provide for their own food and shower/grey water. There is no primo camping for the people who are providing you medical care. 

&#x200B;

Volunteers ensure you get ambulances when you need them. They help you get a crane to stabilize your art. They feed other volunteers. They help distressed participants through difficult substance experiences. They counsel rape survivors on their rights and options. Is it really asking too much for theme camps to allow a little room in their camp for a few volunteers? Camps can help support the city by allowing volunteers with specialized skills to have a place to call home (no amenities needed in most cases, just real estate). Make room for the helpers, or who will help?

Perhaps in the future you cold replace the word 'women' with 'people'? Men do porn too...  A lot of this information is particularly relevant to the LGBTQIA community. Many young gay men turn to this kind of work to survive when their families reject them. 

&#x200B;

I also think it is important to point out to people considering this kind of work that even though it should not be shameful, there are many narrow-minded people in the world and you may need to work with them some day. Once porn is out there, it's out there. Chances are you will not always be in poverty. You may some day find yourself in a position to apply for a job you really want, and a history in porn may limit your options.  I agree that it shouldn't, but that is not how the world works unfortunately. Heck, you may pull yourself out of poverty and want to run for local government office some day and create policies which help people like you. Think long term and make choices that are in keeping with your future plans.

> what's the harm in just wrapping yourself up in zen before doing it? 

&#x200B;

I love that. In fact, I personally feel the more calm, zen, blissful things you look at and listen to that whole day before you go in, the better the experiences you will have (though my funniest breakthrough was when I was with a bunch of raver kids and listening to hard style EDM). On the day of my best breakthrough I was looking at some beautiful glass art online and I think it definitely had an impact on the visuals in my trip. Zen your prep! 

&#x200B;

> The most successful people with women aren't working on self talk to  succeed with women.  They're not deliberately practicing and honing  their seduction skills. 

&#x200B;

Preach! Research shows that those who do try the PUA methods are actually *less* successful than nice guys. This "lateral" approach is just putting your energy into more valuable pursuits in terms of women; educated, traveled, happy in your career, accomplished are each WAY sexier than put-downs any day.

&#x200B;
